---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import AuthorProfile from "../components/AuthorProfile.astro";
import NewsTimeline from "../components/NewsTimeline.astro";
---

<Base wide>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 md:grid-cols-4">
    <aside class="md:sticky md:top-12 md:self-start">
      <AuthorProfile />
    </aside>
    <div class="md:col-span-3">
  <section class="prose-lg max-w-none">
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
      Hello! I'm Jared. I'm a second-year PhD student at the UW Paul G.
      Allen School for Computer Science &amp; Engineering. I am a part of
      the
      <a
        href="https://makeabilitylab.cs.washington.edu/"
        class="underline decoration-accent-600/50 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-accent-700 dark:decoration-accent-400/60 dark:hover:decoration-accent-300"
        >Makeability Lab</a
      >, advised by
      <a
        href="https://jonfroehlich.github.io/"
        class="underline decoration-accent-600/50 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-accent-700 dark:decoration-accent-400/60 dark:hover:decoration-accent-300"
        >Jon Froehlich</a
      >, working to make cities more sustainable and accessible.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed">
      My research interests are in urban informatics and urban data
      understanding, powered by AI and computer vision. Specifically:
    </p>

    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <li>
        📝 Tools for <strong>managing raw, multimodal data</strong> — how
        can we bridge the gap between collecting multimodal data and using
        it in downstream applications?
      </li>
      <li>
        💡 Using AI to <strong>extract insight</strong> — how can AI extract
        insight out of unstructured and multi-dimensional data, and how can
        we make context-aware, personalized systems for urban exploration?
      </li>
      <li>
        🚞 Building <strong>better cities</strong> — how can we surface
        insight about our cities and the people who live in them, and
        present it to policymakers and individuals intuitively?
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed">
      Check out my
      <a
        href="/research"
        class="underline decoration-accent-600/50 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-accent-700 dark:decoration-accent-400/60 dark:hover:decoration-accent-300"
        >research</a
      > and
      <a
        href="/cv_file/hwang_CV.pdf"
        class="underline decoration-accent-600/50 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-accent-700 dark:decoration-accent-400/60 dark:hover:decoration-accent-300"
        >CV</a
      > to see how my interests got to where they are now. Or, if you want
      to chat about research, cities, the PhD program, or anything else,
      reach out by email.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="mt-16">
    <NewsTimeline />
  </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
